<statement>
<p>
Solve the following linear system.  If the system has an infinite number of solutions, parameterize the solution set in terms of the free variables of the original system.</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left\lbrace\begin{array}{ccccccc} {9}{x}\amp-\amp{81}{y}\amp-\amp{36}{z}\amp=\amp{9}\\-{9}{x}\amp+\amp{81}{y}\amp+\amp{36}{z}\amp=\amp-{9}\\{4}{x}\amp-\amp{36}{y}\amp-\amp{16}{z}\amp=\amp{4}\end{array}\right.}</m></p>
<p>
x = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
y = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
z = <fillin characters="20"/>  

</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle{1}+{9}{y}+{4}{z}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{y}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{z}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>

</myopenmath>